\"margin\":0},\"children\":\"This page could not be found.\"}]}]]}]}]],[]],\"forbidden\":\"$undefined\",\"unauthorized\":\"$undefined\"}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"33:I[55169,[\"/_next/static/chunks/ff1a16fafef87110.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/73350e696300078d.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/3a4fb10029fc91d1.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/2166b7d4a87176d4.js\"],\"TOCProvider\"]\n34:I[769,[\"/_next/static/chunks/ff1a16fafef87110.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/73350e696300078d.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/3a4fb10029fc91d1.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/2166b7d4a87176d4.js\"],\"Sidebar\"]\n35:I[47486,[\"/_next/static/chunks/ff1a16fafef87110.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/73350e696300078d.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/3a4fb10029fc91d1.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/2166b7d4a87176d4.js\"],\"ClientWrapper\"]\n36:T1f87,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"import { Disclaimer } from \"../components/Disclaimer.tsx\"\n\n# Best Practices\n\n## Key storage and security\n\n### Never expose private keys\n\nThe keyring contains four private keys. Treat the serialized keyring with the same care as a wallet seed phrase:\n\n- **Use `sessionStorage`** for in-browser apps. Session storage is cleared when the tab closes, minimizing the window during which a stolen key is usable.\n- **Never put the serialized keyring in `localStorage`** unencrypted. LocalStorage persists indefinitely and is accessible to any script running on your origin.\n- **Never transmit the keyring over the network.** All operations that require private keys (signing, decryption) must happen client-side.\n- **Consider an encrypted vault.** For persistent login, encrypt the serialized keyring with a user-derived key (e.g. from a passkey PRF output or a PBKDF2-stretched password) before storing it.\n\n### Prefer passkey derivation\n\nFor browser apps, derive the keyring from a WebAuthn passkey using the PRF extension. This ties key access to the user's authenticator hardware and avoids storing private key material anywhere:\n\n```ts\nimport { createUserKeyringFromPasskey } from \"@anomaorg/anoma-app-sdk\";\n\nconst keyring = createUserKeyringFromPasskey(credential);\n// The keyring is derived fresh on each login — nothing is stored\n```\n\n### Separate storage for the discovery key pair\n\nThe discovery key pair is registered with the Indexer and is less sensitive than the signing/nullifier keys, but it is still a private key. Register it once and never re-register unnecessarily — doing so will not break anything but is wasted work.\n\n## WASM initialization\n\n### Initialize once at app startup\n\n`initWasm()` loads the WebAssembly module. Call it once at application startup before any other SDK calls:\n\n```ts\n// e.g. in your React app entry point or _app.tsx\nimport { initWasm } from \"@anomaorg/anoma-app-sdk\";\n\nawait initWasm();\n```\n\nCalling `initWasm()` multiple times is safe but unnecessarily reloads the module.\n\n### Initialize `TransferBuilder` once and reuse\n\n`TransferBuilder.init()` also loads the WASM module (it calls `initWasm` internally). Create one instance and reuse it across all transfer operations in a session rather than calling `init()` per transaction:\n\n```ts\n// Instantiate once\nconst transferBuilder = await TransferBuilder.init();\n\n// Reuse for all transfers\nconst resolver1 = new ParametersDraftResolver(transferBuilder, keyring);\nconst resolver2 = new ParametersDraftResolver(transferBuilder, keyring);\n```\n\n## Error handling\n\n### Catch `ResponseError` from API clients\n\nAll API clients throw `ResponseError` on non-2xx responses. Check `err.status` for HTTP status codes that require specific handling (e.g. 429 for rate limiting, 500 for backend errors):\n\n```ts\nimport { ResponseError, HttpStatus } from \"@anomaorg/anoma-app-sdk\";\n\ntry {\n  await backend.transfer(parameters);\n} catch (err) {\n  if (err instanceof ResponseError) {\n    if (err.status === HttpStatus.TooManyRequests) {\n      // back off and retry\n    } else if (err.status === HttpStatus.ServerError) {\n      // show a generic error\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Handle `InsufficientResourcesError`\n\n`selectTransferResources` (called internally by `ParametersDraftResolver`) throws `InsufficientResourcesError` when the user does not have enough private balance:\n\n```ts\nimport { InsufficientResourcesError } from \"@anomaorg/anoma-app-sdk\";\n\ntry {\n  const resolved = resolver.build(availableResources, forwarderAddress);\n} catch (err) {\n  if (err instanceof InsufficientResourcesError) {\n    // err.required — the amount the user tried to send\n    // err.available — the amount actually available\n    showError(`Insufficient balance. Required: ${err.required}, Available: ${err.available}`);\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Use `getFirstErrorMessage` in UI error boundaries\n\nWhen surfacing errors to users, use `getFirstErrorMessage` to extract a readable string regardless of whether the error is a `ResponseError`, `ZodError`, or a plain `Error`:\n\n```ts\nimport { getFirstErrorMessage } from \"@anomaorg/anoma-app-sdk\";\n\nconst message = getFirstErrorMessage(err) ?? \"An unexpected error occurred.\";\n```\n\n## Permit2 nonces\n\nPermit2 signatures include a nonce to prevent replay attacks. The nonce must be unique per signature. Using `BigInt(Date.now())` is acceptable for most apps:\n\n```ts\nconst nonce = BigInt(Date.now());\n```\n\nFor higher-frequency applications, maintain a monotonically increasing counter stored in `sessionStorage`, or use `crypto.getRandomValues` to generate a random 128-bit integer.\n\n## Resource polling\n\n### Refresh resources on a fixed interval\n\nResources appear on-chain only after their creating transaction is proven and submitted. The SDK constant `balanceRefetchIntervalInMs` (10,000 ms) is the recommended polling interval for wallet UIs:\n\n```ts\nimport { balanceRefetchIntervalInMs } from \"@anomaorg/anoma-app-sdk\";\n\nsetInterval(() =\u003e fetchAndUpdateResources(), balanceRefetchIntervalInMs);\n```\n\n### Timestamp-filter nullifier queries\n\nTo avoid re-fetching the entire nullifier history on each poll, pass the timestamp of the last known nullifier to `publicNullifiers`:\n\n```ts\nconst nullifiers = await envio.publicNullifiers(\n  TRANSFER_LOGIC_VERIFYING_KEY,\n  lastKnownTimestamp\n);\n```\n\nThis significantly reduces the GraphQL response size for users with long transaction histories.\n\n## Queue load monitoring\n\nBefore prompting the user to confirm a transaction, check the queue load and adjust your UX accordingly:\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  isHeavyLoad,\n  provingGPUs,\n  estimateTransferTimeInSeconds,\n} from \"@anomaorg/anoma-app-sdk\";\n\nconst { processing } = await backend.statsQueue();\nconst heavy = isHeavyLoad(processing, provingGPUs);\nconst estimatedSeconds = estimateTransferTimeInSeconds(parameters);\n\nif (heavy) {\n  showWarning(`The proving queue is under heavy load. Your transaction may take longer than the usual ~${estimatedSeconds}s.`);\n}\n```\n\n## Fee fluctuation tolerance\n\nToken prices used to compute percentage fees can move between the time you call `estimateFee` and the time you submit. The SDK accepts a fee variance of up to 5% (`FeeFluctuationPercentage`). This means:\n\n- Show the estimated fee to users as approximate, not exact.\n- Do not cache fee estimates for more than a few seconds before display.\n- If the backend rejects a transaction due to fee mismatch, re-estimate and re-build.\n\n## Multi-receiver transfers\n\nWhen sending to multiple receivers in one transaction, always call `addReceiver` for all of them before calling `build()`. Adding receivers after `build()` has been called requires creating a new `ParametersDraftResolver` instance:\n\n```ts\nconst resolver = new ParametersDraftResolver(transferBuilder, keyring);\n\n// Add ALL receivers before build()\nresolver.addReceiver({ type: \"AnomaAddress\", userPublicKeys: keys1, quantity: 5_000_000n, token });\nresolver.addReceiver({ type: \"AnomaAddress\", userPublicKeys: keys2, quantity: 3_000_000n, token });\n\n// Then build once\nconst resolved = resolver.build(availableResources, forwarderAddress);\n```\n\n\u003cDisclaimer\u003e\nThe PayloadBuilder.withAuthorization() call signs the Merkle root of all consumed and created resource pairs. If you change the resource set after signing, the signature will be invalid. Always call withAuthorization after build().\n\u003c/Disclaimer\u003e\n\n## Retry logic\n\nThe backend can occasionally return transient errors (network timeouts, 500s during high load). Use `retryMutationsCount` as the recommended retry limit:\n\n```ts\nimport { retryMutationsCount } from \"@anomaorg/anoma-app-sdk\";\n\nlet attempts = 0;\nwhile (attempts \u003c retryMutationsCount) {\n  try {\n    const result = await backend.transfer(parameters);\n    return result;\n  } catch (err) {\n    attempts++;\n    if (attempts \u003e= retryMutationsCount) throw err;\n    await new Promise(r =\u003e setTimeout(r, 2_000 * attempts)); // exponential back-off\n  }\n}\n```\n\nDo not retry transactions that returned `Unprocessable` — the parameters are invalid and retrying will always fail. Only retry on network errors or `500` responses."])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"5:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"x:mx-auto x:flex x:max-w-(--nextra-content-width)\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L33\",null,{\"value\":[{\"value\":\"Key storage and security\",\"id\":\"key-storage-and-security\",\"depth\":2},{\"value\":\"Never expose private keys\",\"id\":\"never-expose-private-keys\",\"depth\":3},{\"value\":\"Prefer passkey derivation\",\"id\":\"prefer-passkey-derivation\",\"depth\":3},{\"value\":\"Separate storage for the discovery key pair\",\"id\":\"separate-storage-for-the-discovery-key-pair\",\"depth\":3},{\"value\":\"WASM initialization\",\"id\":\"wasm-initialization\",\"depth\":2},{\"value\":\"Initialize once at app startup\",\"id\":\"initialize-once-at-app-startup\",\"depth\":3},{\"value\":[[\"$\",\"$1\",\".0\",{\"children\":[\"Initialize \",[\"$\",\"code\",\".1\",{\"className\":\"nextra-code\",\"dir\":\"ltr\",\"children\":\"TransferBuilder\"}],\" once and reuse\"]}]],\"id\":\"initialize-transferbuilder-once-and-reuse\",\"depth\":3},{\"value\":\"Error handling\",\"id\":\"error-handling\",\"depth\":2},{\"value\":[[\"$\",\"$1\",\".0\",{\"children\":[\"Catch \",[\"$\",\"code\",\".1\",{\"className\":\"nextra-code\",\"dir\":\"ltr\",\"children\":\"ResponseError\"}],\" from API clients\"]}]],\"id\":\"catch-responseerror-from-api-clients\",\"depth\":3},{\"value\":[[\"$\",\"$1\",\".0\",{\"children\":[\"Handle \",[\"$\",\"code\",\".1\",{\"className\":\"nextra-code\",\"dir\":\"ltr\",\"children\":\"InsufficientResourcesError\"}]]}]],\"id\":\"handle-insufficientresourceserror\",\"depth\":3},{\"value\":[[\"$\",\"$1\",\".0\",{\"children\":[\"Use \",[\"$\",\"code\",\".1\",{\"className\":\"nextra-code\",\"dir\":\"ltr\",\"children\":\"getFirstErrorMessage\"}],\" in UI error boundaries\"]}]],\"id\":\"use-getfirsterrormessage-in-ui-error-boundaries\",\"depth\":3},{\"value\":\"Permit2 nonces\",\"id\":\"permit2-nonces\",\"depth\":2},{\"value\":\"Resource polling\",\"id\":\"resource-polling\",\"depth\":2},{\"value\":\"Refresh resources on a fixed interval\",\"id\":\"refresh-resources-on-a-fixed-interval\",\"depth\":3},{\"value\":\"Timestamp-filter nullifier queries\",\"id\":\"timestamp-filter-nullifier-queries\",\"depth\":3},{\"value\":\"Queue load monitoring\",\"id\":\"queue-load-monitoring\",\"depth\":2},{\"value\":\"Fee fluctuation tolerance\",\"id\":\"fee-fluctuation-tolerance\",\"depth\":2},{\"value\":\"Multi-receiver transfers\",\"id\":\"multi-receiver-transfers\",\"depth\":2},{\"value\":\"Retry logic\",\"id\":\"retry-logic\",\"depth\":2}],\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L34\",null,{}],[\"$\",\"$L35\",null,{\"metadata\":\"$2:props:children:1:props:children:props:children:props:children:2:props:pageMap:22:frontMatter\",\"bottomContent\":\"$undefined\",\"sourceCode\":\"$36\",\"children\":[\"$L37\",\"$L38\"]}]]}]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"39:I[63894,[\"/_next/static/chunks/ff1a16fafef87110.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/73350e696300078d.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/3a4fb10029fc91d1.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/2166b7d4a87176d4.js\"],\"HeadingAnchor\"]\n37:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"id\":\"nextra-skip-nav\"}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"38:[\"$\",\"main\",null,{\"data-pagefind-body\":true,\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h1\",null,{\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"className\":\"x:tracking-tight x:text-slate-900 x:dark:text-slate-100 x:font-bold x:mt-2 x:text-4xl\",\"children\":[\"Best Practices\",\"$undefined\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"id\":\"key-storage-and-security\",\"className\":\"x:tracking-tight x:text-slate-900 x:dark:text-slate-100 x:font-semibold x:target:animate-[fade-in_1.5s] x:mt-10 x:border-b x:pb-1 x:text-3xl nextra-border\",\"children\":[\"Key storage and security\",[\"$\",\"$L39\",null,{\"id\":\"key-storage-and-security\"}]]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"id\":\"never-expose-private-keys\",\"className\":\"x:tracking-tight x:text-slate-900 x:dark:text-slate-100 x:font-semibold x:target:animate-[fade-in_1.5s] x:mt-8 x:text-2xl\",\"children\":[\"Never expose private keys\",[\"$\",\"$L39\",null,{\"id\":\"never-expose-private-keys\"}]]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"not-first:mt-[1.5em] leading-[1.65em] text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-200\",\"children\":\"The keyring contains four private keys. Treat the serialized keyring with the same care as a wallet seed phrase:\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"className\":\"x:[:is(ol,ul)_\u0026]:my-[.75em] x:not-first:mt-[1.25em] x:list-disc x:ms-[1.5em]\",\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"my-[1em] text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-200 leading-[1.65em]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":[\"Use \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"className\":\"nextra-code\",\"dir\":\"ltr\",\"children\":\"sessionStorage\"}]]}],\" for in-browser apps. Session storage is cleared when the tab closes, minimizing the window during which a stolen key is usable.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"my-[1em] text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-200 leading-[1.65em]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":[\"Never put the serialized keyring in \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"className\":\"nextra-code\",\"dir\":\"ltr\",\"children\":\"localStorage\"}]]}],\" unencrypted. LocalStorage persists indefinitely and is accessible to any script running on your origin.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"my-[1em] text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-200 leading-[1.65em]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Never transmit the keyring over the network.\"}],\" All operations that require private keys (signing, decryption) must happen client-side.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"my-[1em] text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-200 leading-[1.65em]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Consider an encrypted vault.\"}],\" For persistent login, encrypt the serialized keyring with a user-derived key (e.g. from a passkey PRF output or a PBKDF2-stretched password) before storing it.\"]}],\"\\n\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"id\":\"prefer-passkey-derivation\",\"className\":\"x:tracking-tight x:text-slate-900 x:dark:text-slate-100 x:font-semibold x:target:animate-[fade-in_1.5s] x:mt-8 x:text-2xl\",\"children\":[\"Prefer passkey derivation\",[\"$\",\"$L39\",null,{\"id\":\"prefer-passkey-derivation\"}]]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"not-first:mt-[1.5em] leading-[1.65em] text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-200\",\"children\":\"For browser apps, derive the keyring from a WebAuthn passkey using the PRF extension. This ties key access to the user’s authenticator hardware and avoids storing private key material anywhere:\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"data-pagefind-ignore\":\"all\",\"className\":\"nextra-code x:relative x:not-first:mt-[1.25em]\",\"children\":[\"$undefined\",[\"$